**Output format:** Respond with a single valid JSON object only. Do not wrap it in markdown or a code fence. Use exactly these keys:
- **"title"** (string): The story title (e.g. "The Case of the Missing Bracelet").
- **"culprits"** (array of strings): Full name(s) of the character(s) responsible for the crime, as revealed at the end.
- **"characters"** (array of strings): Full names of all other characters with a role (suspects, detective, witnesses, etc.). Do not include culprits here.
- **"locations"** (array of strings): Every distinct location in the story (e.g. rooms, buildings, streets, venues).
- **"clues"** (array of strings): Clues that appear in the story and help solve the mystery or point to the culprit(s). One short phrase or sentence per clue.
- **"items"** (array of strings): Items used as evidence (e.g. objects, documents, physical evidence).
- **"story"** (string): The full narrative in one coherent piece (you may start with the title). It must end with the revelation of the culprit(s).

Example: `{"title": "...", "culprits": ["Name"], "characters": ["Detective X", "Witness Y"], "locations": ["The Manor", "Study"], "clues": ["The broken lock showed signs of..."], "items": ["bloody handkerchief", "letter"], "story": "Paragraphs..."}`

